    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d875">

                <pb facs="1005" n="811" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg811"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 (Potsdam)/7–3145</note>
                <head>No. 875<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by the British
                    Delegation</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-sibling-dates" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-23">Undated</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">U. K. Proposal</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article</hi> 19 <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">of “Economic Principles”</hi></p>
                <p>19. After payment of Reparations enough resources must be left to enable the
                    German people to subsist without external assistance. In working out the
                    economic balance of Germany the necessary means <pb facs="1006" n="812"
                        xml:id="pg812"/> must be provided to pay for imports approved by the
                    Governments concerned.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d875-f1"/> The proceeds of the
                    exports from current production and stocks shall be available in the first place
                    for payment for such imports.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d875-f1" n="1" xml:id="d875-f1-content">
                <p>Another version of this paper, with the same heading, found in the Pauley Files, ends this sentence with the words
                    “approved by the Control Council”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
